---
*Adapted and extended from P. Larson, "Principles of MRI" (MIT License), chapter "FOV and Resolution". Changes: added derivation from comb↔comb and rect↔sinc with continuous-object and stripe-pattern demos, aliasing on analytic and real data, PSF, Gibbs ringing and windowing, hardware relations (gradients, dwell time, bandwidth, off-by-one in phase encoding), a worked design calculator, and readout-oversampling discussion with the knee data. Corrected the original code's unnormalized sinc (the "square" was ~N/π instead of N pixels wide) and the claim that the two test points were 1 pixel apart (they are 4 pixels apart); $FOV_y$ uses the lobe duration $t_y$ (not $\Delta t_y$).*
